  m_Name: Janitor
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  npcName: Marcus Torres
  characterDescription: "Long-time hotel janitor in his 50s who knows every corner
    of the building. \nUsually quiet and methodical, but seems unusually shaken and
    keeps avoiding eye contact tonight."
  initialGreeting: "Evening, detective. Terrible business, this. \nI've been working
    here 15 years and never seen anything like it."
  friendliness: 0.7
  intelligence: 0.6
  patience: 0.9
  openness: 0.4
  reliability: 0.8
  backgroundStory: "Has been struggling financially and started stealing small valuable
    items from guest rooms to sell online. \nRecently escalated to planting listening
    devices to gather business information he could sell to competitors."
  knowledgeTopics:
  - hotel layout
  - master keys
  - guest schedules
  - cleaning procedures
  - building security
  storyKnowledge: 0.5
  storyTriggerWords:
  - cleaning
  - access
  - keys
  - rooms
  - 10:00
  - device
  - Tom
  - violent
  - hiding
  secretInformation: I was in Room 312 at 10:00 PM planting a listening device behind
    the desk to capture Blackwood's business calls. When I heard someone coming up
    the hallway, I hid in the bathroom. Through the keyhole, I saw Tom Bradley pounding
    on the door around 10:20 PM, yelling about some business deal.
  knownEvidence:
  - was inside room 312 at 10:00
  - planted listening device
  - hid in bathroom
  - witnessed Tom's confrontation
  - saw through keyhole
  suspectInformation:
  - om Bradley was extremely violent and angry - he was pounding that door like he
    wanted to break it down
  - Sarah's been acting nervous about money lately - she keeps checking the cash
    drawer
  - Officer Williams got here awfully fast - almost like he was already nearby
  usesEmotions: 0
  uniqueQuirks: "Speaks slowly and methodically. \nKnows everyone's routines and
    schedules. \nDeflects questions about his whereabouts by mentioning his cleaning
    duties."
  customSystemPrompt: 
  maxResponseLength: 3
  usesSlang: 0
  isFormal: 0
  defaultEmotion: neutral
  availableEmotions:
  - neutral
  - happy
  - sad
  - angry
